# Single-page app: every route is served by index.html and matched client-side. Cloudflare Pages
# reads this file; Netlify reads the same rule from netlify.toml. Functions under /api are matched
# before redirects on both, so this does not shadow them.
#
# A missing file under /assets/ would be answered by this rule too, which is wrong: `_headers` marks
# that prefix immutable for a year, so the browser would cache index.html under a JavaScript URL and
# never ask again. `functions/assets/[[path]].ts` turns that case back into a 404. It cannot be
# expressed here, because Pages only honours redirect codes and the 200 rewrite in this file.
/*    /index.html   200
